  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is moving uniformly in a circular path of radius $r$. When it moves through an angular displacement $\\theta$, then the magnitude of the corresponding linear displacement will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Sr9c3",
      "text": "$2 r \\cos \\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Cvy9T",
      "text": "$2 r \\cot \\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "h6wU3",
      "text": "$2 r \\tan \\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "1s7na",
      "text": "$2 r \\sin \\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\ln \\Delta A O B \\quad \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}=\\frac{A B}{A O}$\n$\\Leftrightarrow A O=r)$\n$\\begin{aligned}\nA B &=A O \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\Rightarrow A B=r \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\nA C &=A B+B C \\quad(\\because A B=B C) \\\\\n&=r \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}+r \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\nA C &=2 r \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}\n\\end{aligned}$\nSo, the magnitude of the corresponding linear displacement will be $2 r \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2014_phy_a21.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
